+# SEOmi 0.4.41 — release notes (Release Candidate)
+
+## Summary
+- Pre-release candidate preparation for version 0.4.41. This candidate packages changes integrated and verified by the root manager; final publication remains gated by remote CI verification.
+
+## Added
+- Release provenance and supply-chain integrity: CycloneDX SBOM generation for Node (spec 1.6) and Rust (spec 1.3), cryptographic SHA256SUMS attestation input, multi-platform artifact inventory binding, idempotent retry/rerun handling with fail-closed digest verification, and deterministic toolchain setup in release workflows (#102).
+- Observational Causal Market Impact panel in Signals: project-scoped analysis with full UI localization across all 12 supported locales, explicit non-causal observational disclaimers, and data boundary validations.
+- Desktop runtime E2E test harness hardening: strict exact-origin hermetic desktop test fixture preventing cross-origin leaks during automated test runs.
+- Credential store compatibility: robust interoperability and safe fallback decoding for legacy encrypted secrets/ciphertext across desktop platforms.
+
+## Changed
+- Candidate version bump to 0.4.41 across application metadata (`package.json`, `package-lock.json`, `Cargo.toml`, `Cargo.lock`).
+
+## Notes & Limitations
+- Release Candidate status: candidate preparation only; production release publication and OIDC attestation are gated on full green CI.
+- Dependency upgrade scope: TypeScript 7 latest remains peer-dependency blocked; package updates reflect verified compatible versions rather than unconstrained latest.
+- Scope boundary: pending workstreams (#137, #138) are not included in this candidate baseline.
+
